-- title:
--   Rationality of the geometric exceptional fibres
-- statement:
--   Fix $N_0 \ge 1$ and a prime $q$ with $q \nmid N_0$, and let $\mathfrak X$ be a Deligne–Rapoport model package [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel N₀ q hqN`](def/ModularCurve_DRModelPackageLevel.html#L71) (a proper, flat, locally of finite presentation integral model of the level-$N_0q$ Igusa curve over $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the subring $R_q$ of $\mathbb Q$ localised at $q$, with normal affine sections, a prescribed curve model of the geometric generic fibre with its Galois action and cusp pinnings, and the further data recorded in that structure). Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with a ring map $\rho_O : R_q \to O$ whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $q$, let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$ and $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa$ a ring map. Assume the site hypotheses $H$: the set of nodes (the fibre product of the two $\mathfrak X$-components over $\kappa$) is finite, oriented crossing charts exist, the étale-neighbourhood hypothesis holds, the crossing points $n \mapsto \mathrm{xpt}(n)$ are pairwise distinct and closed in the $O$-model, and the model hypotheses for $q$ and $O$ hold; assume also that each distinguished section $\xi_j$ lands in the open set $X_0$ of the chart input, the complement of the crossing points. Write $e_n$ for the thickness (width) attached to a node $n$, $Y \to \operatorname{Spec} O$ for the glued resolution, and for an index $v$ let $\mathrm{comp}(v)$ be the corresponding ideal sheaf datum on $Y$ with its closed subscheme. Then for every node $n$ and every $i < e_n - 1$ there exist a curve model $M$ of $\kappa(T) =$ `RatFunc κ` over $\kappa$ — a scheme $M.C$, integral, proper and smooth of relative dimension $1$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\kappa$, together with an isomorphism of $\kappa(T)$ with its function field compatible with the base, a bijection between its closed points and the places of $\kappa(T)/\kappa$ matching stalks with valuation subrings, and the property that every finite set of points lies in one affine open — and a morphism $e$ from $M.C$ to the fibre product of the closed immersion of the exceptional component $\mathrm{comp}(\mathrm{inr}(n,i))$ into $Y$ followed by $Y \to \operatorname{Spec} O$ with $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{to}\kappa)$, such that $e$ is an isomorphism and $e$ followed by the second projection equals $M.\mathrm{toBase}$.
--
--   This is the field of the resolved Deligne–Rapoport model package asserting that the exceptional components produced by resolving a crossing of the $q$-fibre of $X_0(N_0q)$ have geometric fibre over $\kappa$ a rational curve, i.e. a projective line; only the strict transforms retain level-dependent geometry. It is used in the assembly [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageLevel_and_dRResolvedModelChartsLevelRam`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageLevel_and_dRResolvedModelChartsLevelRam), and is deduced from the two-affine-line cover of the toric resolution together with the criterion identifying a fibre supported at one point with a residue-field spectrum.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_V3AsmLevel_exc_rational.lean

